WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.000
Rules decide where queries go.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.737
A forwarding rule names one
domain and its target addresses.

3
00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:08.317
The most specific matching rule wins,

4
00:00:08.317 --> 00:00:12.312
and a rule overrides a private
hosted zone of the same name.

5
00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:16.587
A rule for the root, a single
dot, forwards almost everything.

6
00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:20.359
System rules carve a subdomain
back out of a forwarding rule,

7
00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:25.037
so it resolves locally, and delegation
rules handle delegated subdomains.

8
00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:28.625
Rules are shared through
AWS Resource Access Manager.

9
00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:33.737
The receiving account associates them with
its VPCs but can't change or delete them.

10
00:00:33.737 --> 00:00:36.905
Profiles go further,
bundling zones, rules,

11
00:00:36.905 --> 00:00:41.612
firewall rule groups and logging
settings, one Profile per VPC.

12
00:00:41.612 --> 00:00:47.779
Private hosted zones answer only inside
associated VPCs, up to 300 per zone,

13
00:00:47.779 --> 00:00:53.300
and an empty match returns NXDOMAIN,
with no fallback to public DNS.
